---
/**
 * /what-applies — narrows a money question and says what to ask.
 *
 * Not a calculator and not an answer. It shows what actually decides a
 * situation, what is settled, what genuinely is not, and which kind of
 * professional resolves the rest.
 */
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.svelte';
import { SITUATIONS } from '../lib/situations';
---

<Shell
  title="What applies to me"
  description="Work out what actually decides your money question — what is settled, what is not, and who to ask. General information, not advice about your situation."
  branch="home"
  width="wide"
>
  <PageHeader
    title="What applies to me"
    subtitle="Pick the closest situation. You will get what usually decides it, what is settled, what is not, and who to ask."
    branch="home"
    backHref="/"
    backLabel="Home"
  />

  <div class="px-5 md:px-0 pb-16">
    <!-- Said once, at the top, before anyone reads a word of the content. -->
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-clay-300 bg-clay-50/60 px-5 py-4 mb-9 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        <strong class="text-text-primary">This is general information, not advice.</strong>
        Every one of these depends on facts a web page cannot see — where you work, what
        your Nation's agreements say, what is written in a trust. It is here to narrow the
        question and tell you what to ask. Take your own situation to a professional who
        can look at it properly.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 md:grid md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-4">
      {
        SITUATIONS.map((s) => (
          <a
            href={`#${s.id}`}
            class="group block rounded-xl bg-surface-card border border-stone-200 px-5 py-4
              hover:border-clay-300 hover:bg-clay-50/40 transition-colors"
          >
            <p class="font-semibold text-[15px] leading-snug group-hover:text-clay-700 transition-colors">
              {s.question}
            </p>
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 flex flex-col gap-14">
      {
        SITUATIONS.map((s) => (
          <section id={s.id} class="scroll-mt-24 max-w-3xl">
            <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">{s.question}</h2>
            <p class="text-text-secondary leading-relaxed mb-7">{s.opening}</p>

            <div class="mb-6">
              <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold text-stone-400 tracking-widest uppercase mb-3">
                What usually decides it
              </h3>
              <ul class="list-none pl-0 m-0 flex flex-col gap-2">
                {s.decidedBy.map((item, i) => (
                  <li class="flex gap-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">
                    <span class="text-text-muted tabular-nums shrink-0">{i + 1}.</span>
                    <span>{item}</span>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-xl border-l-[3px] border-sage-400 bg-sage-50/50 px-5 py-4 mb-4">
              <h3 class="text-[10px] font-bold tracking-[0.14em] uppercase text-sage-700 mb-2">
                Generally settled
              </h3>
              <ul class="list-none pl-0 m-0 flex flex-col gap-2">
                {s.settled.map((item) => (
                  <li class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-text-primary">{item}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-xl border-l-[3px] border-clay-400 bg-clay-50/50 px-5 py-4 mb-4">
              <h3 class="text-[10px] font-bold tracking-[0.14em] uppercase text-clay-700 mb-2">
                Genuinely unsettled
              </h3>
              <ul class="list-none pl-0 m-0 flex flex-col gap-2">
                {s.unsettled.map((item) => (
                  <li class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-text-primary">{item}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
              <p class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-3 leading-relaxed">
                Where something is unsettled, be careful of anyone who sounds certain about
                it.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-xl bg-stone-100 px-5 py-4 mb-5">
              <h3 class="text-[10px] font-bold tracking-[0.14em] uppercase text-stone-500 mb-2">
                Who to ask
              </h3>
              <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-text-primary">{s.ask}</p>
            </div>

            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              {s.reading.map((r) => (
                <a
                  href={r.href}
                  class="rounded-lg bg-surface-card border border-stone-200 hover:border-clay-300
                    px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-colors"
                >
                  {r.label}
                </a>
              ))}
            </div>
          </section>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mt-14 pt-6 border-t border-stone-200">
      Nothing here is a recommendation about your own money, and none of it replaces
      someone looking at your actual situation. If a page and a professional disagree,
      the professional has seen facts this page has not.
    </p>
  </div>
</Shell>
